[META]
framework: claude-framework
file_id: CONSTRAINTS
class: custom
version: 1.0.0

[CONSTRAINTS_MEMORY]
[CONSTRAINT_1]
rule: Never store pointers from frame_allocator across frames
why: Frame allocator memory is invalidated at frame start (ds::frame_allocator_reset())
how_to_apply:
  - If you need data across frames, use other allocators (std::make_shared, pool_resource)
  - For frame data: std::pmr::vector<T>(ds::frame_allocator()) is safe within frame
  - Always read comment at alloc site: "frame temp" vs "persistent"

[CONSTRAINT_2]
rule: Always reserve() when count is known
why: Avoids grow-and-copy within bump allocator (wastes memory + performance)
how_to_apply:
  std::pmr::vector<rnd::render_packet> packets(ds::frame_allocator());
  packets.reserve(estimated_count); // BEFORE pushing

[CONSTRAINT_3]
rule: deallocate() is a no-op on linear allocator
why: Memory only reclaimed on reset() (bump allocation design)
how_to_apply:
  - Individual deallocate() calls don't free memory
  - Only bulk reset() at frame boundary reclaims
  - Don't create tight alloc/free loops in frame (use pool_resource instead)

[CONSTRAINTS_LOGGING]
[CONSTRAINT_4]
rule: Never use std::cout, std::cerr, or std::cin
why: engine_log.h provides formatted, filterable per-category logging (spdlog backend)
how_to_apply:
  #include "engine_log.h"
  Macros: egLOG/egLOG_INFO, egLOG_WARN, egLOG_ERROR, egLOG_TRACE, egLOG_DEBUG
  First arg = category string, then std::format args:
    egLOG_WARN("resource", "not found: {}", tag);
  source: core/core/common/logger/engine_log.h (macros defined L46-62)

[CONSTRAINTS_CODE_STYLE]
[CONSTRAINT_5]
rule: C++20 only, no compiler extensions
why: Cross-platform compatibility, maintainability
how_to_apply:
  - No __attribute__, __declspec, #pragma pack (use standard equivalents)
  - No compiler-specific builtins
  - Test on multiple platforms

[CONSTRAINT_6]
rule: Tabs (size 4) for indentation everywhere
why: Project-wide consistency
how_to_apply:
  - Configure editor: spaces=off, tab_size=4
  - All files .hpp, .cpp, CMakeLists.txt, .md use tabs

[CONSTRAINT_7]
rule: snake_case for all identifiers
why: Consistency across codebase
how_to_apply:
  - Variables: my_variable
  - Functions: my_function()
  - Classes: my_class (rare, prefer structs for data)
  - Enums: MY_ENUM_VALUE (exceptions: UPPER_CASE for macros)

[CONSTRAINTS_ARCHITECTURE]
[CONSTRAINT_8]
rule: No global state in performance-critical code
why: Prevents cache contention, simplifies testing
how_to_apply:
  - Render loop: zero statics, all data in structs
  - ECS systems: dependencies via registry context
  - Per-frame allocations: use frame_allocator, not statics

# Owner-accepted architectural decisions (Windows+OpenGL now behind backend-agnostic RHI, GLFW behind platform::window,
# own graphics backends only, GLSL portability rules, explicit ECS phases, m_ prefix): docs/roadmap/ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW.md §9

[CONSTRAINT_9]
rule: ImGui::End() must be called regardless of Begin() return value
why: Begin/End must stay paired even when the window is collapsed/hidden; Begin() result only gates drawing
how_to_apply:
  if (ImGui::Begin("Name")) {
    // panel content
  }
  ImGui::End();   // always
  Same for BeginChild/EndChild. BeginPopup*/BeginMenu/BeginTable: End* only if Begin* returned true.
  source: Editor/code/editor_system/panels/edt_panel_base.cpp render()

[CONSTRAINT_10]
rule: Use res::tag for all resource identification
why: Prevents cache misses, enables hot-reload
how_to_apply:
  auto mesh = resources.require<mesh_resource>(res::tag{"res://models/backpack"});  // resources: res::resource_system& injected
  res::get_system() is legacy (being phased out for DI) — no new uses
  Never: hardcode filenames in component, always use descriptors
  source: core/core/resource/res_system.h require<T>/require_sync<T> (L170-178)

[CONSTRAINT_11]
rule: Always use engine_assert.h (ASSERT_MSG, ASSERT_FAIL)
why: Provides stack traces, assert dialogs, debug info
how_to_apply:
  #include "engine_assert.h"
  ASSERT_MSG(condition, "message");
  ASSERT_FAIL("error");
  NOT: assert() macro or C std assert

[CONSTRAINTS_ECS]
[CONSTRAINT_12]
rule: Components are POD structs, no virtual functions
why: Cache efficiency, memcpy safety
how_to_apply:
  struct transform_component {
    glm::mat4 matrix;
    glm::vec3 position;
    // no virtual ~, no callbacks
  };

[CONSTRAINT_13]
rule: Systems inherit ecs::system_interface
why: Required base for ecs::system_factory::register_automatic_system
how_to_apply:
  struct my_system : ecs::system_interface { /* state only */ };
  // system_interface has NO update()/initialize() — it is just a virtual dtor.
  // The per-frame logic is a free or member function whose args (entt::view,
  // ecs::bind_res<ID,T>, ...) are auto-resolved by the organizer:
  sfactory.register_automatic_system<&my_system::tick, my_system>("my_system", inst);
  source: core/core/ecs/ecs_system_interface.hpp, ecs_system.h

[CONSTRAINT_13B]
rule: Automatic system dispatch supports world IDs 0-4 only (max 5 worlds)
why: registration_dispatcher::dispatch is a hard-coded switch (case 0..4);
     world_id > 4 hits ASSERT_MSG(false, "World ID > 4 not supported...")
how_to_apply:
  - Keep level world count <= 5, or expand the switch in ecs_system.h
  - world_salt is just a size_t wrapper, NOT a fixed-size limit by itself
  source: core/core/ecs/ecs_system.h registration_dispatcher::dispatch (L80-99)

[CONSTRAINT_13C]
rule: World order is desc order; derive parallel world arrays from one ordered source
why: scn::level::for_each_world iterates std::unordered_map<string,world> in HASH
     order — it does NOT preserve desc/insertion order. With >=2 worlds, building
     editor arrays (world_descs/world_names/worlds_systems_list) from for_each_world
     desyncs the parallel arrays.
how_to_apply:
  - Treat the ordered world_descs vector as single source of truth for order
  - Derive names + per-world systems via edt::derive_world_arrays (index-aligned)
  - populate_worlds_from_level is the single build point on load
  source: core/engine/scene/level/scn_level.h for_each_world (L46-57);
          Editor/code/editor_system/controller/edt_level_controller.h derive_world_arrays

[CONSTRAINTS_RESOURCES]
[CONSTRAINT_14]
rule: Never bypass resource cache
why: Prevents duplicate loads, enables hot-reload
how_to_apply:
  ✅ auto h = resources.require<T>(tag);   // res::resource_system& via DI; res_handle<T>
  ❌ new T(); load from disk directly

[CONSTRAINT_15]
rule: Resources use VFS (res:// or memory://)
why: Enables mods, asset packing, runtime replacement
how_to_apply:
  res:// = filesystem path (default protocol)
  memory:// = runtime-created data
  Never embed paths in code, always use tags
gotcha: single-arg res::tag{"..."} PARSES the protocol out of the string —
  the string must contain "protocol://" or protocol/path/name slices are wrong.
  Use the 2-arg form res::tag{"res", "path"} or res::tag::make(path) to prepend
  the default protocol; 2-arg form asserts the path has no "://" already.
  source: core/core/resource/res_tag.h ctor (L20-40)

[CONSTRAINTS_DESCRIPTORS]
[CONSTRAINT_16]
rule: Scene truth is in level_desc, not code
why: Data-driven architecture, runtime flexibility
how_to_apply:
  - Don't spawn entities in code
  - Use prefabs and level descs
  - Editors change descs, code reads them

[CONSTRAINT_17]
rule: Descriptor inheritance: never circular deps
why: Serialization and validation
how_to_apply:
  OK: level → world → prefab → prefab_node
  VETO: world references level, prefab references world

[CONSTRAINTS_RENDERING]
[CONSTRAINT_18]
rule: Render target tags are per-camera
why: Multiple worlds need independent targets
how_to_apply:
  Editor injects: __editor_depth_rt, __editor_tp_accum_rt, etc.
  Fallback to legacy tags for backward compat

[CONSTRAINT_19]
rule: Frame allocator must reset every frame
why: Prevents memory bloat, GC-like semantics
how_to_apply:
  Frame start: ds::frame_allocator_reset()
  → clears all frame-temp data
  → next frame has clean slate
